<http://data.silknow.org/object/61ba88dd-6216-3051-8042-40b403ba04a3/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Long gauze shawl with 3.75 inch bands of pale blue and white. The warp is pale blue and the weft is twisted white silk and untwisted pale blue. The twisted silk fringe is knotted into the two ends and has two rows of lattice, and alternates pale blue and white silk areas as broad as the bands. Meant to be worn folded double to produce the illusion of moiré silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/61ba88dd-6216-3051-8042-40b403ba04a3> .

